JWT `exp` field = seconds since epoch. `Date.now()` = **milliseconds**.

Off by 1000x → expired tokens always look valid (exp < now/1000, but you compare exp < now → always true for recent tokens).

**Fix:**

```js
// Wrong
if (token.exp < Date.now()) throw new Error('Expired');

// Right
if (token.exp < Date.now() / 1000) throw new Error('Expired');
// or
if (token.exp * 1000 < Date.now()) throw new Error('Expired');
```

**Better — use library that handles this:**

```js
import jwt from 'jsonwebtoken';

// Verifies signature + expiry automatically
const payload = jwt.verify(token, SECRET); // throws if expired
```

`jwt.verify` handle unit mismatch, clock skew, all edge cases. Manual check = footgun.
